<pre>Case A: Both agree — linear = monotone, no outliers.
Case B: Pearson drops sharply, Spearman barely changes → outlier exposed.
Case C: Spearman ≈ 1.0 (perfect monotone), Pearson misses the exponential curve.
</pre>
